                        ],
                        "form": "den Rufmord"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "8f27a851-500c-43ea-a39b-75fe4c7ad42a",
                        "entry_id": "1985ee33-4f17-37cd-b29f-192b9be87118",
                        "tags": [
                            "accusative",
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "die Rufmorde"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "733c6abe-dc89-3fcd-9dc6-2a7a24f69ea9",
                        "entry_id": "1985ee33-4f17-37cd-b29f-192b9be87118",
                        "glosses": [
                            "schwere üble Nachrede, die das Ansehen einer Person nachhaltig beschädigen kann"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e156d913-8967-44f3-bc19-cadd3eccec51",
                                "sense_id": "733c6abe-dc89-3fcd-9dc6-2a7a24f69ea9",
                                "text": "„Offen sprach er davon, eine Sanierung sei nicht möglich. Im Nachhinein wird der Manager froh sein können, wenn er nicht wegen versuchten Rufmords und Verleumdung von einem Quelle-Beschäftigten belangt wird.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "373be898-1319-4106-9a81-3154e1ab277d",
                                "sense_id": "733c6abe-dc89-3fcd-9dc6-2a7a24f69ea9",
                                "text": "„Wichtig war, dass er hier in dieser Limousine, die ihn aus dem Land bringen sollte, den Genossen die Geschehnisse der vergangenen Stunden im Detail darlegte, auch, um dem Rufmord durch Dollfuß vorzugreifen.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2fc3db5c-5e97-4a08-9e15-fcfdafe5388c",
                        "source_entry_id": "1985ee33-4f17-37cd-b29f-192b9be87118",
                        "source_sense_id": "733c6abe-dc89-3fcd-9dc6-2a7a24f69ea9",
                        "source_sense_description": "schwere üble Nachrede, die das Ansehen einer Person nachhaltig beschädigen kann",
                        "target_lang_word": "calumny",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "calumny",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b51156c-42f6-30dd-8e39-b7171a411db1",
                                        "entry_id": "ad8a8091-7a6f-35a6-a24c-273c0b5604be",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A false accusation or charge brought to tarnish another's reputation or standing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c62df672-043b-4114-be28-8a8705eb96b2",
                                                "sense_id": "5b51156c-42f6-30dd-8e39-b7171a411db1",
                                                "text": "He [Thomas Howard, 4th Duke of Norfolk] mentioned to her [Elizabeth I of England] the rumour, which was ſpread of his marriage with the Scotch Queen [Mary, Queen of Scots]; he complained of it as a groundleſs calumny; and diſclaimed all thoughts of that kind, with many expreſſions full of contempt, both for Mary's character, and dominions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1618b0d-15d6-4a6b-86e4-6c6db7fc11e1",
                                                "sense_id": "5b51156c-42f6-30dd-8e39-b7171a411db1",
                                                "text": "To publish all malicious calumnies against an individual with an intent to defame him, is a wrong on the part of the calumniator, and an injury to the individual, for which the law affords redress. To write or print these calumnies is such an aggravation of the crime, as to constitute an offense against the government, and the author of the libel is subject to the additional punishment which may be inflicted under an indictment."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fe955d5f-f2a0-4685-a34e-a42b5c9d6e4b",
                                                "sense_id": "5b51156c-42f6-30dd-8e39-b7171a411db1",
                                                "text": "The First Consul looked upon her as his child. It was only in that country so fertile in the inventions of scandal, that so foolish an accusation could have been imagined, as that any feeling less pure than paternal affection actuated his conduct toward her. The vile calumny met with the contempt it merited."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64a2bc64-b906-4108-9c53-104abf410968",
                                                "sense_id": "5b51156c-42f6-30dd-8e39-b7171a411db1",
                                                "text": "He [James Westland] lost his temper when Mr. [Pherozeshah Merwanjee] Mehta spoke in his vigorous manner of the defects of the Civil Service, and complained bitterly that Mr. Mehta was introducing a new spirit in the discussions in the Legislative Council, and ended by accusing him of uttering a calumny. When, however, the speeches of the two were published, the public was in a position to judge who it was that had uttered a calumny."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "582f7296-9324-460c-9e92-1a3ea312cf07",
                                                "sense_id": "5b51156c-42f6-30dd-8e39-b7171a411db1",
                                                "text": "We are convinced that the fine reputation and the worthy role of the German soldier, despite all the calumnies of recent years, are still cherished among our people and will remain so."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9275b37d-6804-33d7-8a58-c905d1879846",
                                        "entry_id": "ad8a8091-7a6f-35a6-a24c-273c0b5604be",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Falsifications or misrepresentations intended to disparage or discredit another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88d701bf-29f1-4014-bd7c-cc9bd0811ed8",
                                                "sense_id": "9275b37d-6804-33d7-8a58-c905d1879846",
                                                "text": "Accusations of abuse were pure extortive calumny in a malicious bid to make money."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18eb0231-7f90-41e9-b59a-73be297138e4",
                                                "sense_id": "9275b37d-6804-33d7-8a58-c905d1879846",
                                                "text": "Thus have I frielie, in reverence and love, schewit my opinion in this matter, and that privatlie to your self alone, to consider it mair deiplie, without bitternes or upbraiding calumnie to thame who sie and hes socht out this mater mair warelie, whose harts I trust ze sal find far from calumnie or seiking praise to them selfs by reproche of uthers,[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c30b29f-9f03-42ce-9add-41f53b0e57f0",
                                                "sense_id": "9275b37d-6804-33d7-8a58-c905d1879846",
                                                "text": "If thou doſt marry, Ile giue thee / This plague to thy dowry: / Be thou as chaſte as yce, as pure as ſnowe, / Thou ſhalt not ſcape calumny, to a Nunnery goe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "871a21f0-8084-4ee4-9014-158a1277653b",
                                                "sense_id": "9275b37d-6804-33d7-8a58-c905d1879846",
                                                "text": "And quhairas ʒour Ma[jesty] is informed, that theſe who wer appoynted to proſequut the Lord Maxwell hes keipit companie with him, theaſe that hes commandement of ʒour Ma[jesty]s Guairdis humlie craves tryall of that calumnie;[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "87bfd54f-52d7-44d6-896a-3587b5eafcde",
                                                "sense_id": "9275b37d-6804-33d7-8a58-c905d1879846",
                                                "text": "In ſhort, no Inſtruments or Methods of Calumny, and Defamation will be left unemployed to cruſh the Man, who has the Courage to oppoſe the Errors, which Avarice, and Self-Intereſt combine to eſtabliſh."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d453e98a-12f5-4b95-ba62-fb95d49884a0",
                                                "sense_id": "9275b37d-6804-33d7-8a58-c905d1879846",
                                                "text": "There meet two rivals of Neptunian race, / Hoſtilities begin with fierce grimace: / In ſcorn, contempt, in oaths and calumny, / In virulence, and vile contumely, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77aedb87-1f83-4a31-a08c-b92e33c8450f",
                                                "sense_id": "9275b37d-6804-33d7-8a58-c905d1879846",
                                                "text": "Stephen, the first martyr of the Church, was a victim of calumny. And calumny is worse than a sin; calumny is a direct expression of Satan."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "calumny",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3070d941-cc36-3bd2-8a1a-8b26f5df09c1",
                                        "entry_id": "9e16f596-50f4-35e8-908c-645ccc7931f1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make false accusations or levy false charges against a person with the intent to tarnish that person's reputation or standing; to calumniate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "formal",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e769fa56-0b81-49a9-9b84-c329650a21f6",
                                                "sense_id": "3070d941-cc36-3bd2-8a1a-8b26f5df09c1",
                                                "text": "His [Dominieus Dietrich's] memory has been basely calumnied by many German historians."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "68fada4d-94e5-4eb6-82ab-8e89f58d38ee",
                                                "sense_id": "3070d941-cc36-3bd2-8a1a-8b26f5df09c1",
                                                "text": "However, the Priests of the idols, not content with persecuting Christians, began to calumny them; the Philosophers, finding a Religion that preached humility unrewarding, joined their Priests. Ridicule and insults were showered […] on the new Sect from all sides."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77bb1ad5-35da-4093-8c97-2530dec57373",
                                                "sense_id": "3070d941-cc36-3bd2-8a1a-8b26f5df09c1",
                                                "text": "It is this coalition that seeks to tear the Republic apart, by ceaselessly calumnying the people of Paris and all the representatives whom it has honoured with its trust …"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4759961a-1666-46af-903f-0271d1536828",
                                                "sense_id": "3070d941-cc36-3bd2-8a1a-8b26f5df09c1",
                                                "text": "He rails, he piles on the abuse, he calumnies without any sense of decency or restraint, and his gloomy character makes him see everything as black."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "979f4e58-2c81-467c-a386-83e7aa855728",
                        "source_entry_id": "1985ee33-4f17-37cd-b29f-192b9be87118",
                        "source_sense_id": "733c6abe-dc89-3fcd-9dc6-2a7a24f69ea9",
                        "source_sense_description": "schwere üble Nachrede, die das Ansehen einer Person nachhaltig beschädigen kann",
                        "target_lang_word": "character assassination",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "character assassination",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b0e9ac1-4c77-3f26-9ae3-a933577ee7c6",
                                        "entry_id": "464198e3-f92b-302a-9d74-9311b027ac29",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A malicious discourse designed to damage the reputation of someone."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c6702b77-51b6-4c53-98cb-5ef6f628e745",
                                                "sense_id": "7b0e9ac1-4c77-3f26-9ae3-a933577ee7c6",
                                                "text": "For months, Dati warned she would refuse to stand aside. Now she has stunned the political class with an open letter to Fillon in Le Monde, a scathing character assassination accusing him of the \"lone ambition\" of a disillusioned political elite, of doing politics in a way that \"never favoured women\" and stopping ethnic-minority candidates from progressing at elections. She said he was committing \"a sad mistake\" in trying to run in Paris."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2c2d7cc9-f506-4615-83ca-3fcaa4f51a07",
                        "source_entry_id": "1985ee33-4f17-37cd-b29f-192b9be87118",
                        "source_sense_id": "733c6abe-dc89-3fcd-9dc6-2a7a24f69ea9",
                        "source_sense_description": "schwere üble Nachrede, die das Ansehen einer Person nachhaltig beschädigen kann",
                        "target_lang_word": "diffamation",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "diffamation",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e295ca6-336c-3952-8418-465b93d84de9",
                                        "entry_id": "433ee9c8-283e-3083-86fe-8374a4d804dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Action de diffamer ou résultat de cette action."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "026cd704-0003-44e6-a20f-dba3430b5944",
                                                "sense_id": "0e295ca6-336c-3952-8418-465b93d84de9",
                                                "text": "Être en butte à de lâches diffamations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "64313f38-f517-4a01-aed8-ea385f00ba35",
                                                "sense_id": "0e295ca6-336c-3952-8418-465b93d84de9",
                                                "text": "Il n’a pu souffrir une si cruelle diffamation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d64af9c-ca0b-4d84-84ea-b6f76f184fff",
                                                "sense_id": "0e295ca6-336c-3952-8418-465b93d84de9",
                                                "text": "Se rendre coupable de diffamation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b82ca472-4773-46f1-a549-f5bc9102eb71",
                                                "sense_id": "0e295ca6-336c-3952-8418-465b93d84de9",
                                                "text": "La question de la liberté d’expression n’est pas compliquée. Mis à part la diffamation et l’appel à la violence, rien ne devrait être interdit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d1d106e8-b8d7-34f1-a8a5-d74452c5cb29",
                                        "entry_id": "433ee9c8-283e-3083-86fe-8374a4d804dc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "En droit, l’allégation ou l'imputation d’un fait qui porte atteinte à l’honneur ou à la considération de la personne à laquelle le fait est imputé."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f3620669-5104-409d-b0a7-32d20a778610",
                                                "sense_id": "d1d106e8-b8d7-34f1-a8a5-d74452c5cb29",
                                                "text": "C’est là ce qui constitue le délit de diffamation, délit qui absorbe la calomnie, puisque le plaignant n’est obligé de prouver que la réalité de la diffamation et que le défendeur n’est pas en droit de lui opposer la vérité des faits."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d85612d-776d-4635-9220-0d700ea69d6d",
                                                "sense_id": "d1d106e8-b8d7-34f1-a8a5-d74452c5cb29",
                                                "text": "Le droit de la diffamation, qui, on s’en rend compte aisément, peut entrer en collision frontale avec le droit de la liberté d’expression, possède des caractéristiques différentes selon les pays démocratiques concernés."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14ed717b-595d-49a2-a48e-fe6b4dce697f",
                                                "sense_id": "d1d106e8-b8d7-34f1-a8a5-d74452c5cb29",
                                                "text": "Ce lundi, se tient le procès en diffamation intenté par l’ex-maire de Drancy contre la journaliste Eve Szeftel pour son livre Le Maire et les Barbares, dans lequel elle dénonçait notamment les pratiques clientélistes de Jean-Christophe Lagarde."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
